<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25467" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Labdăcus</span></b> , i,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λάβδακος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a king of Thebes,
				father of Lāius</i>, <i><span class="en">Sen.
				Herc Fur. 495</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id.
				Phoen. 53</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lab-dăcĭus</span></b> , a, um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to</i>
			
			<i>Labdacus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dux,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Eteocles, so called after his grandfather
						Lāius</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 2, 210</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Labdăcĭdes</span></b> , ae,
			m., <i>a male descendant of Labdacus, a
				Labdacide;</i> applied to <i>Polynīces</i> as grandson of Laius, <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 6,
				450</span></i>. —<i>Plur.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Labdăcĭdae</span></b> ,
				ārum, m., <i>the Thebans</i>, <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 9, 777</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10,
			36</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
